{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "fdp-order-service-collection",
		"name": "FDP - order-service (sync + async demo)",
		"description": "Exercises order-service end to end: real OpenFeign calls to customer-service and restaurant-service (sync), Resilience4j circuit breaker/retry/bulkhead protecting both, and a real RabbitMQ publish (async) on every placement/cancellation. Every domain service binds a dynamic, OS-assigned port (`server.port=0`) and is reached exclusively through `api-gateway` on `:8080` -- this collection's `...ServiceUrl` variables already point at the gateway, never at a service's own (unadvertised) port. Requires `discovery-server` (:8761, fixed), `api-gateway` (:8080, fixed), and `customer-service`/`restaurant-service`/`order-service` all running and registered in Eureka — see RUNNING.md. Import the sibling `FDP.postman_environment.json` and select it before running.\n\nRun order: **1. Get Tokens**, then **2. Prerequisite Setup** (self-contained — registers its own customer/address/restaurant/menu item so this collection doesn't depend on the other two having run first), then **3. Place & Manage Orders**, then **4. Negative / Security Tests**.\n\nTo see the resilience story for yourself: stop `restaurant-service` (see RUNNING.md's \"Stopping a backgrounded/jar-run service\" — its port is dynamic, look it up via Eureka first), re-run \"Place Order\" — expect a clean `503 SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE` in a few seconds, not a hang. Restart it, wait ~10s (the circuit breaker's configured wait-duration-in-open-state), and it recovers on its own.\n\nTo see the async story: after \"Place Order\" succeeds, open RabbitMQ's management UI (http://localhost:15672, login fdp/fdp) → Queues → `order-events.inspection` → Get messages — a real `OrderPlacedEvent` JSON payload is sitting there.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"item": [
		{
			"name": "1. Get Tokens (Keycloak)",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Get Customer Token",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"const body = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.test('token issued', () => pm.expect(body.access_token).to.be.a('string'));",
									"pm.environment.set('customerToken', body.access_token);"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "urlencoded",
							"urlencoded": [
								{
									"key": "grant_type",
									"value": "password"
								},
								{
									"key": "client_id",
									"value": "{{clientId}}"
								},
								{
									"key": "username",
									"value": "{{customerUsername}}"
								},
								{
									"key": "password",
									"value": "{{customerPassword}}"
								}
							]
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{keycloakUrl}}/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token",
							"host": [
								"{{keycloakUrl}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"realms",
								"{{realm}}",
								"protocol",
								"openid-connect",
								"token"
							]
						}
					}
				},
